/*
:name: loop_reduce_or
:type: equiv
:verilog_top: loop_reduce_or.top
:pyrope_top: top
*/

// A `for` loop whose body is an OR-REDUCTION, with the loop index in the slice
// bounds: r[i] = |a[4i+3 .. 4i]. Two lowerings meet here that the standalone
// fixtures cover only apart -- `reduce_or` has the `#|` cell with no loop, and
// the `loop_roll_*` group has the loop with no reduce.
//
// The index is the load-bearing part. The loop lowers ROLLED by default (one
// `__loop0` Sub replicated four times with `i` as a RUNTIME port), so the slice
// `(i*4)..=((i*4)+3)` becomes a dynamic Get_mask rather than four constant
// ones, and the bound analysis emits a `descending bit-range select (hi < lo)`
// warning it cannot discharge for a runtime `i`. That warning is the reason
// this pair exists: the emitted hardware must still be right, and only the
// golden can say so. `loop_reduce_or_1.prp` is the same source UNROLLED, which
// pins rolled == unrolled on the Pyrope-vs-Pyrope axis.
//
// It is also the fixture for the `#|` SYNTHESIS gap: `pass.abc` has no
// combinational bit-blast for the `ror` cell ("cell 'ror' has no combinational
// bit-blast yet"), so this design proves but does not yet map. When it does,
// its netlist is comparable against this golden.

pub mod top(a:u16) -> (r:u4@[0], any:u1@[0]) {
  mut acc:u4 = 0
  for i in 0..<4 {
    acc#[i] = unsigned(a#|[(i * 4)..=((i * 4) + 3)])
  }
  r   = acc
  any = unsigned(acc#|[0..=3])
}
